  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis change ensures that rapids between levels in 3D Pocket stop at feed height above the last cut floor instead of reaching the floor with zero margin (#3671):\n- Updated `camcraft_motion::machining3d::descent::from`: on levels with a previous cut, the descent starting plane adds `ap.plunge_height` (the operation's feed height) to `mat_top(lvl, a)`, capped under the traverse plane `lvl.tz`.\n- The rapid between levels stops at this feed height above the prior floor; the remaining descent into the next level is fed (e.g. helical feed or linear ramp).\n- Regenerated the example catalog case `3d/rough-finish` (`rough-finish.camproj` and `rough-finish.nc`). The lowest rapid in `3D Pocket1` now stops at Z12 (2 mm above the Z10 floor) instead of Z10.\n- Added pinning test `interlevel_rapid_stops_at_feed_height_above_prior_floor` in `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/case_3d_rough_finish.rs`.\n- Updated `examples/catalog/3d/rough-finish/README.md`.\n- Added decision record `docs/decisions/3671-3d-pocket-interlevel-rapid-margin.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `cargo xtask catalog --case 3d/rough-finish` ran cleanly and updated the project and NC program.\n- In `rough-finish.nc`, all rapid moves between levels now stop with a 2.0 mm margin above the previous cut floor.\n- All 3 test cases in `catalog_3d_rough_finish` pass.\n- All modified files remain under 400 lines.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/case_3d_rough_finish.rs`:\n  - `catalog_3d_rough_finish::interlevel_rapid_stops_at_feed_height_above_prior_floor`\n  - `catalog_3d_rough_finish::regenerates`\n  - `catalog_3d_rough_finish::rebuilds`\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- Full workspace test suite (targeted catalog and motion tests passed).\n\nChangelog: 3D Pocket: stop the rapid between levels at feed height above the last cut floor.\n\nFixes #3671\n",
